# SYNTHETIC fixture (Pattern 34) — fake values only, no real credentials.
# Covers DEFAULT_INCLUDE's `**/*.env.*`, which this engine was missing until
# 2026-07-29 while the canonical Python tool had it. `**/*.env` does NOT match
# a suffixed env file, so `.env.local` / `.env.production` — where a real leak
# most often sits — were skipped entirely.
#
# Named `app.env.local` rather than `.env.local` so the file survives the
# global/user gitignores that commonly carry a bare `.env*` rule; the leading
# dot shape is covered at runtime by the CLI smoke instead (it writes a real
# `.env.local` into a temp dir). No quotes, so generic_secret_assignment does
# not co-fire and this stays a clean 1:1 case.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE
